      "Correspondence & Testimonials — Manchester, 19 November — Dear Julian, following our panel discussion on contemporary labor markets, I wanted to share two testimonies gathered during my fieldwork on non-standard employment. For decades after the Second World War, industrialized economies anchored social citizenship in the standard employment relationship: a full-time, open-ended contract offering predictable income, paid leave, health coverage, and pension security. Today, corporate outsourcing, algorithmic scheduling, and the proliferation of temporary, part-time, and gig-economy arrangements have steadily eroded that protective norm, creating a growing class of workers trapped in chronic economic insecurity.",
