"Correspondence & Testimonials — Geneva, 22 January — Dear Martin, following our conference on international humanitarian law and environmental displacement, I am sending you two accounts from my recent field missions illustrating why climate-induced migration has become one of the defining moral and legal tests of our century. Unlike sudden political upheavals that often dominate headlines, climate disruption displaces people through both catastrophic storms and slow-onset erosion—rising seas, prolonged droughts, salinized farmland, and lethal heatwaves—forcing tens of millions to abandon ancestral homes.",
