"Correspondence & Testimonials — New York, 11 March — Dear Nadia, following our symposium on multilateral governance, I wanted to share two testimonies from practitioners working inside international organizations that illustrate the profound strain confronting global institutions today. Founded in the aftermath of the Second World War to prevent global conflict, stabilize the world economy, and uphold human rights, the multilateral system—anchored by the United Nations, international financial bodies, and specialized health and climate agencies—is increasingly struggling to respond decisively to cascading twenty-first-century crises.",
