"Closing of letter to Nadia — As both Samuel and Carla demonstrate, the crisis of international institutions is not proof that multilateralism has failed; rather, it is a warning that inherited twentieth-century institutions must be modernized for a multipolar, interdependent age. Reforming Security Council voting procedures, democratizing global financial governance, establishing predictable funding for humanitarian and climate public goods, and strengthening enforcement of international law are indispensable if global institutions are to meet the defining emergencies of our time."
