"Addressing mental health as a central public health priority therefore demands comprehensive, preventive, and community-anchored reform. Integrating mental healthcare into universal primary health services, training community health workers to deliver evidence-based psychosocial support, regulating workplaces and digital environments to protect psychological well-being, and addressing root socioeconomic stressors such as housing security and social isolation are essential. True public health is indivisible: there can be no genuine health without mental health."
