      "Personal Account by Moussa, 23, a Trained Electrical Technician from a Small Town in West Africa: 'I graduated from my vocational training program with excellent grades, but there are hardly any formal industrial businesses in my region that hire skilled workers. Many of my former classmates struggle in the informal sector, relying on insecure casual jobs without social security or opportunities for career advancement. Furthermore, our school curricula lacked practical content and direct connections with businesses. When young people make considerable efforts but still see no future opportunities, frustration grows, and for many, risky migration appears to be the last resort.'",
